A||||3||Pretender||deck lid???
Z||000000||Pretender||04-07-99||09:15 PM||||what keeps the deck lid up?...how do i fix this?...i do have the factory wing on my 88gt, is the the weight of the wing keeping it from staying up?<br>
Z||000001||PaUL||04-07-99||09:20 PM||||the deck lid is held up by 2 torsion bar like springs.  These are very hard to remove because of the tension. My decklid doesnt stay up either with the rear wing on. I once took the wing off and then the lid stayed up.<br>Ive seen strut type keep ups on a few sites made especially for the fiero. try this site:http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/<br>
Z||000002||theogre||04-07-99||10:18 PM||||This is a common problem with alot of these options no mater what brand car it is. (I had a 73 maverick with a factory option "spoiler" that would whack you every chance it got. My 86 caravan need both gas tubes replaced.... it won't stay up at all even w/o a wing.)<p>I'd agree with paul. Add an auxilary lift. If I recall you need to tell rodney if you are just boosting a week torque rod, or eliminating them comleatly. Adding the lift is both easier, and safer, than trying to remove the springs.
